# Python build artefacts, scoped to backend/ — the only Python root here.
#
# These came from the stock Python template, where they are unanchored and so
# match a directory of that name at *any* depth. `lib/` therefore excluded the
# frontend's `src/lib/`, and because a gitignored file is silently absent rather
# than reported, utils.ts, useAutoSize.ts and releaseSeen.ts were never
# committed at all. Every deployment build then failed on fifteen copies of
# "Cannot find module '../../lib/utils'" while the files sat present locally,
# which is why it looked like a build problem rather than a missing file.
#
# `build/`, `dist/`, `var/` and `parts/` are equally ordinary frontend
# directory names and were one `src/` folder away from doing the same thing.
backend/build/
backend/develop-eggs/
backend/dist/
backend/downloads/
backend/eggs/
backend/.eggs/
backend/lib/
backend/lib64/
backend/parts/
backend/sdist/
backend/var/
backend/wheels/
backend/share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

